#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Attaches the delegation note to the start of every session.
set -euo pipefail

cat <<'JSON'
{"hookSpecificOutput":{"hookEventName":"SessionStart","additionalContext":"Shared assistants are available in this workspace. Delegate to them by default.\n\n- finder: locate files, docs, tickets, or records\n- researcher: read external documentation and report back\n- builder: complete a scoped piece of work end to end\n- analyst: spreadsheets, data pulls, and reducing long output\n- checker: independently verify finished work before you report done\n\nThis session is running an expensive model. Its job is to plan, dispatch, integrate, and decide. It is not to read files, write drafts, run commands, or grind through data. Hand that work out.\n\nDelegating is the default, not the exception. Do work here only when it is a single trivial step, or when handing it off is genuinely impossible. When nothing else fits, use builder.\n\nWhen a task has independent pieces, dispatch them in parallel in one message rather than one at a time. That is what lets a multi-part project finish in a single session.\n\nAssistants proceed on stated assumptions rather than stopping to ask, so read the assumptions in their reports before integrating.\n\nYou own completion. They finish their pieces; you finish the project. Do not report done until every part is done, and use checker to confirm rather than trusting your own summary."}}
JSON
